      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'm really sorry to hear about your accident. It's strongly advised to avoid putting any substances like tea tree oil or butter on the burn as they may cause further irritation or infection. Instead, gently run cool (not cold) water over the burn for about 10-20 minutes to help reduce pain and swelling, then cover with a sterile gauze tightly wrapped around a bowl to prevent irritation. Seek medical attention right away to get proper treatment. Make sure not to pop any blisters as they protect against infection. Is there anything else I can assist you with?",
